====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|poetic|archaic|or|obsolete}} [[high#Adjective|High]], [[tall#Adjective|tall]], [[towering#Adjective|towering]]; also, [[position#Verb|positioned]] in a high [[place#Noun|place]]; [[high-up]], [[lofty]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Virgil|Aeneis|passage='''Sublime''' on these a tower of steel is reared.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}}
## Of an [[aspect#Noun|aspect]] of [[art#Noun|art]] or [[nature#Noun|nature]]: [[cause#Verb|causing]] [[awe#Noun|awe]] or [[deep#Adjective|deep]] [[respect#Noun|respect]] due to its [[beauty#Noun|beauty]] or [[magnificence]]; [[awe-inspiring]], [[impressive]].
##: {{ux|en|'''sublime''' scenery}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=John Munro|title=A Trip to Venus|chapter=VI|chapterurl={{fullurl:s:en:A_Trip_to_Venus/Chapter_VI}}|passage=We had entered the clouds. For half-an-hour we were muffled in a cold, damp mist, and total darkness, and had begun to think of going indoors when, all at once, the car burst into the pure and starlit region of the upper air. A cry of joyous admiration escaped from us all. The spectacle before us was indeed '''sublime'''.}}
## Of [[flight#Noun|flight]]: [[ascending#Adjective|ascending]], [[soaring#Adjective|soaring]].
## Of [[language]], [[style#Noun|style]], or [[writing#Noun|writing]]: [[express#Verb|expressing]] [[opinion]]s in a [[grand#Adjective|grand]] [[way#Noun|way]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1718|author=w:Matthew Prior|title=Poems on Several Occasions|chapter=To Dr. Sherlock, On His Practical Discourse Concerning Death|url=https://www.eighteenthcenturypoetry.org/works/pmp18-w0540.shtml|passage=Easy in words thy style, in sense '''sublime'''.}}
## Of a [[person#Noun|person]] or their [[action#Noun|actions]] or [[quality#Noun|qualities]]: [[intellectually]], [[morally]], or [[spiritually]] [[superior#Adjective|superior]].
##: {{ux|en|a '''sublime''' deed}}
##* {{RQ:Longfellow Voices|page=13|passage=Know how '''sublime''' a thing it is, / To suffer and be strong.}}
## Of an [[office#Noun|office]] or [[status]]: very high; [[exalted#Adjective|exalted]]; also, {{non-gloss definition|[[use#Verb|used]] (often [[capitalize]]d as '''Sublime''') as an [[honorific#Noun|honorific]] to [[refer#Verb|refer]] to someone of high office or status, especially the [[Ottoman#Adjective|Ottoman]] [[sultan]]; or to things [[associated#Adjective|associated]] with such a person.}}
## Of a [[thing]]: [[consummate#Adjective|consummate]], [[perfect#Adjective|perfect]]; {{lb|en|informal|loosely}} [[excellent#Adjective|excellent]], [[marvellous]], [[wonderful#Adjective|wonderful]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|year_published=1995|author=Richard Klein|isbn=0330340166|publisher=Picador|location=London|title=Cigarettes are sublime|page=62|passage=Cigarettes are poison and they taste bad; they are not exactly beautiful, they are exactly '''sublime'''.}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|poetic|archaic}} Of a person: [[dignified#Adjective|dignified]], [[majestic]], [[noble#Adjective|noble]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1842|author=w:Thomas De Quincey|title=Cicero|journal=Blackwood's Edinburgh Magazine|passage=the '''sublime''' Julian leader}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|poetic|archaic}} Of a person: [[haughty]], [[proud]].
##* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=V|canto=VIII|stanza=30|passage=countenance '''sublime''' and insolent}}
##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=4|passage=His fair large Front and Eye '''ſublime''' declar'd / Abſolute rule;}}
## {{lb|en|informal|chiefly in the negative}} [[complete#Adjective|Complete]], [[downright#Adjective|downright]], [[utter#Adjective|utter]].
##: {{synonyms|en|absolute|out-and-out}}
##: {{ux|en|He is behaving like a '''sublime''' idiot.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}}
## {{lb|en|figurative}}
### [[elevate#Verb|Elevated]] by [[joy#Noun|joy]]; [[elated#Adjective|elated]].
###* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=Samson Agonistes|page=96|passage=While thir hearts were jocund and '''ſublime''', / Drunk with Idolatry, drunk with Wine,}}
### Of a [[substance#Noun|substance]]: [[purified#Adjective|purified]], [[refined#Adjective|refined]]; hence, of the highest quality.
## {{lb|en|poetic|postpositive}} Of [[arm#Noun|arms]]: [[lift up|lifted up]], [[raise#Verb|raised]].
## {{lb|en|pathology}} Of [[breathing#Noun|breathing]]: very [[laboured#Adjective|laboured]].

